"""Task, execution and local relation prompts for the documented MAGNET adaptation."""
PROBLEM = '''Describe the supplied public task and ORIGINAL reference observations for grouping tasks that may share a workflow. Do not solve, use previous answers, or invent hidden information. Return family, problem_structure, target, critical_constraints, visual_requirements, normalized_description. Family must use the supplied vocabulary. Preserve distinguishing structure (e.g. Latin-square row/column uniqueness vs multiplication relations; grouped vs stacked bars; date vs identifier). Replace example names, dates, years and measured values with typed placeholders unless they are structural mathematical constants. Describe category/series structure rather than data values. normalized_description must summarize task structure and required transformation in under 90 English words. Unknown facts remain unknown; do not guess the answer page or a method.'''
PROCEDURE = '''Summarize ONLY operations actually evidenced in the supplied historical execution. Return procedure_description and operations. Each operation has operation, step_index, quote. quote is an EXACT short verbatim substring of the supplied step text; step_index is zero-based. For code, cite the actual API call or expression. Operations within one model_response are text/code segments, NOT separate verified tool executions. Do not invent OCR, search, regex, algebra steps or repairs merely because they could solve the problem. Parameterize historical answers/data in procedure_description; keep the original quote only as provenance. Use at most 5 distinct meaningful operations and under 90 words in procedure_description. If evidence is insufficient use an empty operations array and explain the limitation in procedure_description.'''
ANCHORED_PROCEDURE = '''Summarize ONLY the actual operations evidenced by the supplied numbered ORIGINAL trajectory fragments. Return procedure_description (the reusable method, not the answer) and operations, each with operation and evidence_id. Choose exact supplied evidence IDs; do not rewrite quotations. Preserve execution/text order. Use at most five distinct meaningful operations, one per selected evidence ID. Parameterize concrete names, answers, dates, measured values and coordinates in operation summaries. Describe transformations such as setting up a relation, computing component areas, drawing bars or mapping labels; do NOT enumerate the old numerical results. Source fragments are evidence of what was written or coded, not proof every intermediate statement is correct. Never invent search/OCR/regex/tool actions or successful repairs. An operation within one response is NOT an independently executed tool step. If unsupported return no operations.'''
COMPRESS = '''Shorten normalized_description to under 65 English words without changing its task structure, target or constraints. Do not add a solution, historical answer, example name or date. Return normalized_description only.'''
WORKFLOWS = '''Extract at most THREE distinct reusable workflows jointly demonstrated by the supplied source records. Use their task structures, actual operations and exact evidence quotes. Each workflow has title, problem_description, procedure_description, applicability, exclusions, parameters, steps, source_ids, support. Preserve semantic operations; replace source-specific values with parameters. Every step must be supported by an operation in at least TWO DISTINCT sources. support contains one row per step_index and source_id, with operation_index pointing to the supplied source operation. Do not cite unrelated snippets, invent a successful action, pad generic observe/analyze/answer steps, or use duplicate source IDs as support. Keep 3 to 5 meaningful steps. If no common ordered workflow is supported, return workflows: []. Different strategies remain separate. Do not derive a new strategy from task similarity alone.'''
ALIGNED_WORKFLOWS = '''Extract at most three reusable workflows shared by ALL supplied source records. Every workflow has title, problem_description, procedure_description, applicability, exclusions, parameters, steps, support. Use 3 to 5 meaningful ordered operations. For each step_index, support.operations_by_source must map EVERY supplied source id to the actual operation_index demonstrating this step. Do not invent operations, use a quote about another action, pad generic observe/analyze/answer steps, or use one source to stand in for another. Operations must remain in their source order without repeated operation indices. Parameterize historical values. If the sources do not demonstrate such a common workflow, return workflows: []. Do not invent a new solution or an executed repair. Different valid methods are separate workflows.'''
VERIFY_STEP = '''Check whether the EXACT quoted historical operation and its supplied context support the candidate workflow step. Assess semantic entailment, not topic similarity. Return supported and reason. Reject invented actions, broader claims, unstated conditions and conclusions justified only by an aggregate success score. A matching identifier alone is not support. If uncertain return supported=false.'''
VERIFY_BATCH = '''Check EVERY numbered item independently. Does its exact quoted historical operation semantically support the proposed common workflow step under the supplied task conditions? Return checks with exact id, supported and a short reason. Topic similarity or a matching identifier is insufficient. Reject broader invented actions, unstated transformations, proposed repairs and claims justified only by an aggregate success score. If uncertain use supported=false. Do not assume one supported item proves another. Return each id exactly once.'''
CANDIDATE_DESCRIPTIONS = '''Write short retrieval descriptions for EACH supplied historical memory candidate. Return descriptions with exact id, problem_description (task structure, target, applicability) and procedure_description (actual ordered operations). Both descriptions together must be under 140 English words. Parameterize example data, names and years; retain mathematical structure, chart type, conditions and DIFFERENT methods. Do not invent missing steps or change the method. For visual memories describe the component's supported function, not just its appearance. Do not claim candidate content has been independently verified. Preserve all input ids exactly once.'''
RELATIONS = '''Compare ONE new memory candidate with EACH supplied historical candidate. Return assessments with exact id, relation and reason. relation is equivalent, alternative_strategy, shared_subroutine, conflict, unrelated or uncertain. equivalent requires the SAME reusable function, compatible applicability and the SAME core ordered method; only wording or instance values may differ. Same task/topic is insufficient. Different methods, extra meaningful steps, general/special-case scope or complementary visual functions are NOT equivalent. Partial overlap is shared_subroutine. If evidence is ambiguous use uncertain. Do not merge scopes by union, invent evidence or infer equivalence transitively. Be conservative about deletion. Assess every supplied id once.'''
INSPECT_CROP = '''Read ONLY the supplied crop. Return visible_text (literal readable characters only), visible_objects (literal objects/lines/shapes), and clipped_or_ambiguous. Do not guess the larger image, complete a cut-off character, infer an invisible number or use a historical description. A blank crop, grid intersection or partial black stroke does not establish a whole digit. Mark clipped_or_ambiguous=true for content that cannot be clearly recognized. JSON only.'''
MATCH_CROP = '''Does the independently observed crop actually show the proposed component? Return supported and reason. Compare the proposed object/observation with the blind crop reading. Partial glyphs, blank areas, isolated grid lines or uncertain content cannot support a claimed readable number or field. Do not use the full source image or historical answer to fill missing pixels. If uncertain reject.'''
FAMILIES = {
    'mathvision': ['latin_square','multiplication_grid','geometry','algebra','combinatorics','probability','data_analysis','other','unknown'],
    'vision2code': ['bar_chart','line_chart','scatter_plot','pie_chart','table_document','geometry_diagram','chemical_structure','graph_network','spatial_scene','other','unknown'],
    'mpdocvqa': ['year','date','identifier','person','organization','amount','count','other','unknown'],
}
